<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Simultaneous equations — line meets parabola</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the simultaneous equations \[ y = {@line@}, \qquad y = {@para@}. \]</p>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Equate the two expressions for \(y\) and rearrange into the form \(x^2 + bx + c = 0\).</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] \(= 0\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Solve this quadratic. Give the set of \(x\)-values, for example \(\{-1, 4\}\).</p>
<div>\(x \in \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>c)</strong> Hence give both solutions as coordinate pairs \([x, y]\), listed as a set, for example \(\{[-1, 2], [4, 7]\}\).</p>
<div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution.</h3>
<p>At a solution of the simultaneous equations, both equations give the <strong>same value of \(y\)</strong>. So we set the two right-hand sides equal, which gives a quadratic equation in \(x\):</p>
\[ \begin{align*} {@para@} &= {@line@}\\ {@quadexpr@} &= 0\\ {@(x-r1)*(x-r2)@} &= 0. \end{align*} \]
<p>So \(x = {@r1@}\) or \(x = {@r2@}\). Substitute each value into the linear equation to find the matching \(y\), and check it in the quadratic one:</p>
<ul>
<li>When \(x = {@r1@}\): \(y = {@y1@}\), and \(({@r1@})^2 + ({@cc@}) = {@y1@}\) as well.</li>
<li>When \(x = {@r2@}\): \(y = {@y2@}\), and \(({@r2@})^2 + ({@cc@}) = {@y2@}\) as well.</li>
</ul>
<p>The solutions are \(({@r1@}, {@y1@})\) and \(({@r2@}, {@y2@})\). They are the two points where the line meets the parabola:</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="The line y = {#line#} and the parabola y = {#para#}, meeting at ({#r1#}, {#y1#}) and ({#r2#}, {#y2#}).">
[[jsxgraph width="380px" height="320px"]]
(function() {
  var L = function(x){ return ({#mm#})*x + ({#kk#}); }, P = function(x){ return x*x + ({#cc#}); };
  var pts = [[{#r1#},{#y1#}],[{#r2#},{#y2#}]];
  var xs = pts.map(function(p){return p[0];}), ys = pts.map(function(p){return p[1];});
  var xmin = Math.min.apply(null, xs) - 2.5, xmax = Math.max.apply(null, xs) + 2.5;
  var ymin = Math.min(0, Math.min.apply(null, ys)), ymax = Math.max(0, Math.max.apply(null, ys));
  for (var t = xmin; t <= xmax; t += (xmax - xmin)/100) { var v = P(t); if (v < ymax + 6) ymax = Math.max(ymax, v); ymin = Math.min(ymin, v); }
  var pad = (ymax - ymin)*0.1 + 1;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[xmin, ymax + pad, xmax, ymin - pad], axis:true, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false});
  b.create('functiongraph', [P], {strokeColor:'#1f5fa8', strokeWidth:2});
  b.create('functiongraph', [L], {strokeColor:'#e67e22', strokeWidth:2});
  for (var i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {
    b.create('point', pts[i], {name:'', size:4, fixed:true, color:'#c0392b'});
  }
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
